## Brief-derived requirements and strict implementation boundary

The screenshots establish the operational intent very clearly. The problem statement says the enterprise cannot reliably determine where an application is actually running, which data centre is actively servicing traffic, and which components are active versus merely deployed or on standby. The brief also says this is not merely a reporting problem, but a data availability, correlation, and control problem. It further says a simplified application model is acceptable, representative data sources may be mocked, and teams are **not expected** to integrate every enterprise platform or solve platform-specific edge cases.

