The 48-hour hackathon plan should stay ruthless.

| Time block | Deliverable |
|---|---|
| Day one morning | Create repo, DB schema, adapter interfaces, rules YAML, FastAPI skeleton |
| Day one afternoon | Implement CMDB adapter, Prometheus/OpenShift adapter, canonical ID resolver |
| Day one evening | Implement MongoDB adapter, first DecisionSnapshot path, basic API responses |
| Day two morning | Build React operator view, evidence drill-down, stale/unknown indicators |
| Day two afternoon | Add AppDynamics adapter, end-to-end demo data, snapshot refresh flow |
| Day two evening | Tests, screenshots, demo script, deployment polish, discovery registry form |

A four-week production roadmap should look like this.

| Week | Milestone |
|---|---|
| Week one | Stabilise schema, complete CMDB/AppDynamics/Prometheus/Mongo/MSSQL adapters, add auth and role-based access |
| Week two | Add Oracle, Kafka, IBM MQ live adapters; improve identifier reconciliation; add snapshot diffing |
| Week three | Production hardening: retries, backoff, secrets handling, audit logging, performance tuning, SLO dashboards |
| Week four | Add optional graph projection, richer evidence exploration, natural-language explainability layer, source-onboarding workflow |

The test plan and acceptance criteria should map directly to the brief.

| Test area | Acceptance condition |
|---|---|
| Deterministic vs derived | UI and API clearly label each evidence item as authoritative or derived |
| Freshness | every evidence item has `observed_at`, `collected_at`, and stale/fresh status |
| Correlation model | the system materialises `application -> component -> asset -> location` |
| Runtime answer | at least one application demo shows where each major component is running |
| Traffic answer | the system shows which site is actively taking traffic |
| State answer | for a stateful component, the system shows which site owns writable state |
| Missing data | missing signals are shown explicitly |
| Conflicts | fresh conflicting authoritative signals force `CONFLICT` or `UNKNOWN`, never green |
| Cognitive load | operator can understand the answer without reading raw telemetry first |
| Explainability | evidence panel shows which data was used, which was missing, how correlation worked, and how confidence was computed |

The demo should be short and operational.

| Step | Action | What judges should see |
|---|---|---|
| Intro | open one application | single consolidated application view |
| Runtime | show component/site matrix | clear runtime footprint |
| Traffic | show active site(s) | traffic posture separated from deployment presence |
| State | show Mongo or MSSQL ownership | writable-state authority made explicit |
| Evidence | open evidence drill-down | supporting, missing, and conflicting signals |
| Failure mode | age one source or inject conflict | `STALE`, `LOW`, or `UNKNOWN`, not guesswork |
| Discovery | submit one new source proposal | alignment with the brief’s discovery requirement |

The main risks are semantic, not just technical.

| Risk | Why it matters | Mitigation |
|---|---|---|
| Identifier mismatch | same runtime object appears differently across tools | explicit native IDs + canonical IDs + mapping tables |
| Semantic overreach | “active” means different things in DB, MQ, Kafka, LB | per-source question authority map |
| Stale data | old evidence can look valid | TTL + freshness factor + visible timestamps |
| Conflicting authoritative sources | drift or lag can produce contradictory answers | hard conflict gate and evidence drill-down |
| Over-automation | LLM-style summaries may invent certainty | rules-only decision engine |
| Adapter sprawl | too many integrations for 48 hours | strict MVP cut and common adapter contract |
| Environment access | real enterprise APIs may not be reachable in time | mock mode allowed by the brief |

Phase 2 should add two things only after the MVP is stable. The first is **graph projection**, not graph-first storage: project snapshots and evidence into Neo4j or Neptune once graph exploration becomes a real need. The second is **AI explainability**, but only as a narrative layer over already-computed evidence and decisions. The model may explain *why* the engine returned LOW or UNKNOWN; it must not decide runtime truth itself. For derived topology aids, the OTel service-graph connector is useful but should remain corroborative because it infers edges from traces rather than establishing authoritative ownership. citeturn13view2turn9search7turn9search1turn16view1

